div:

This page provides a list of the FHIR artifacts defined as part of this implementation guide.


Behavior: Operation Definitions {% capture grouping_desc %}These are custom operations that can be supported by and/or invoked by systems conforming to this implementation guide.{% endcapture %}
    {{ grouping_desc | markdownify}}





               Export WHONET Flat File

            {% capture desc %}Exports AMR DiagnosticReport data as a WHONET-compatible flat file or GLASS submission file. The operation flattens the FHIR resource graph (DiagnosticReport -> OrganismObservation -> SusceptibilityObservation) into isolate-centric rows suitable for WHONET import or WHO GLASS batch upload.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}





Structures: Resource Profiles {% capture grouping_desc %}These define constraints on FHIR resources for systems conforming to this implementation guide.{% endcapture %}
    {{ grouping_desc | markdownify}}





               Botswana AMR DiagnosticReport

            {% capture desc %}Bundles AMR culture results into one comprehensive report. References top-level observations (gram stain and organism identifications). Susceptibility and special test results are accessed via OrganismObservation.hasMember.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Encounter

            {% capture desc %}Captures the clinical encounter context for AMR surveillance: ward type (inpatient/outpatient/ICU), admission date, department, and facility. Required for WHONET export and GLASS hospital-acquired vs community-acquired classification.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Gram Stain Observation

            {% capture desc %}Records gram stain results for specimens in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Organism Identification Observation

            {% capture desc %}Records organism identification results from culture in Botswana AMR surveillance. Acts as the parent observation for susceptibility and special test results via hasMember.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Patient

            {% capture desc %}Patient profile for Botswana AMR surveillance capturing essential demographics{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Special Test Observation

            {% capture desc %}Records special AMR test results (ESBL, Carbapenemase, D-Zone, MRSA) in Botswana AMR surveillance. Should be referenced from the parent OrganismObservation via hasMember.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Specimen

            {% capture desc %}Specimen profile for Botswana AMR surveillance with required collection details{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Susceptibility Observation

            {% capture desc %}Records S/I/R (and optional MIC) for a single antibiotic test on a specimen. Should be referenced from the parent OrganismObservation via hasMember.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}





Structures: Extension Definitions {% capture grouping_desc %}These define constraints on FHIR data types for systems conforming to this implementation guide.{% endcapture %}
    {{ grouping_desc | markdownify}}





               Specimen Collection Location

            {% capture desc %}Ward or facility location where specimen was collected{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}





Terminology: Value Sets {% capture grouping_desc %}These define sets of codes used by systems conforming to this implementation guide.{% endcapture %}
    {{ grouping_desc | markdownify}}





               Botswana AMR AST Method

            {% capture desc %}Antimicrobial susceptibility testing methods used in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Antibiotic Susceptibility LOINC

            {% capture desc %}Collection of LOINC codes for antibiotic-susceptibility tests (MIC panel and individual drugs){% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Gram Stain Results

            {% capture desc %}Gram stain results used in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Interpretation

            {% capture desc %}Only Susceptible, Intermediate, or Resistant{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Organism Identification Methods

            {% capture desc %}Methods used for organism identification in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Organism ValueSet

            {% capture desc %}Organisms identified in Botswana AMR surveillance. Includes all descendants of SNOMED CT 'Organism' (410607006) plus local codes for organism combinations that labs report together.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Special Tests

            {% capture desc %}Special antimicrobial resistance tests performed in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Specimen Collection Sites

            {% capture desc %}Anatomical sites where specimens are collected for Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Specimen Type VS

            {% capture desc %}Specimen types used in Botswana AMR data collection, reusing v3-SpecimenType codes{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Test Result Status

            {% capture desc %}Status values for test results in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Ward Type

            {% capture desc %}Ward/location types for AMR surveillance, aligned with WHONET location type and GLASS origin classification{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}





Terminology: Code Systems {% capture grouping_desc %}These define new code systems used by systems conforming to this implementation guide.{% endcapture %}
    {{ grouping_desc | markdownify}}





               Botswana AMR Local Identification Method Codes

            {% capture desc %}Local codes for identification methods used in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               Botswana AMR Local Organism Codes

            {% capture desc %}Local codes for organism combinations and complex designations used in Botswana AMR surveillance{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}





Terminology: Concept Maps {% capture grouping_desc %}These define transformations to convert between codes by systems conforming with this implementation guide.{% endcapture %}
    {{ grouping_desc | markdownify}}





               WHONET Antibiotic Codes to LOINC Susceptibility Codes

            {% capture desc %}Maps WHONET antibiotic codes to LOINC susceptibility test codes. Derived from the AMR R package (https://github.com/msberends/AMR). Contains 271 WHONET antibiotic codes with LOINC mappings. Note: equivalence is 'relatedto' because one WHONET antibiotic code maps to multiple LOINC codes representing different test methods (MIC, disk diffusion, etc.).{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               WHONET Antibiotic Codes to SNOMED CT Substance Codes

            {% capture desc %}Maps WHONET antibiotic codes to SNOMED CT substance concept IDs. Derived from the official LOINC-SNOMED CT Ontology (September 2025) by tracing LOINC susceptibility codes through their SNOMED observable entity representations to the Component (704320005) relationship, which identifies the substance being tested. Contains 213 authoritative antimicrobial mappings.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               WHONET Antibiotic Codes to WHO ATC Classification

            {% capture desc %}Maps WHONET antibiotic codes to WHO ATC (Anatomical Therapeutic Chemical) codes. Derived from the AMR R package (https://github.com/msberends/AMR). Contains 374 WHONET antibiotic codes with ATC mappings.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}




               WHONET Organism Codes to SNOMED CT

            {% capture desc %}Maps WHONET organism codes to SNOMED CT concepts. Derived from the AMR R package (https://github.com/msberends/AMR) which integrates WHONET organism codes with SNOMED CT mappings. Contains 4995 WHONET organism codes.{% endcapture %}
{{ desc | markdownify}}





